{
  "response": "I’m sorry you’re dealing with this — let’s get it sorted. Because multiple cards are PIN‑locked we have to investigate all of them before we can unlock any, and I’ll need to verify your identity before accessing your card status or taking actions.",
  "next_steps": [
    "Please confirm which two of the following you can provide now for verification: date of birth (MM/DD/YYYY), email address on file, phone number on file, or your mailing address on file. (We only need two.)",
    "After verification I will: 1) check the PIN-locked status for each card, 2) look for any automatic escalation triggers (e.g., security hold, a card recently reported stolen, or 3+ prior locks), and 3) follow the PIN Lock Investigation Protocol to determine whether we can unlock, reset PINs, freeze, or escalate to the security team.",
    "If you’ve noticed any recent suspicious activity, or if any of the cards were reported lost/stolen, tell me now so I can prioritize that during the investigation.",
    "If you prefer to speak with a human immediately instead of going through verification and the investigation here, say so and I’ll arrange a transfer."
  ],
  "prompt": "Which two verification fields would you like to provide (DOB, email, phone, or address)? Also tell me whether any card was reported lost/stolen or if you’ve seen suspicious transactions."
}
